rch Scientist - Audio & Speech\n\n→\n\n05\n\n### Research Scientist - Multimodal\n\n→\n\n06\n\n### Knowledge Engineer\n\n→\n\nFor any questions, please contact us via email: mimo@xiaomi.com--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://mimo.xiaomi.com/zh)\nciteturn4849search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; 2025年10月21日 ... 2025年9月19日 ... ### MiMo: Unlocking the Reasoning Potential of Language Model – From Pretraining to Posttraining ... 11\n\n# 你好，我是 MiMo\n\n# HELLO, I'M MiMo\n\n关于我\n\n欢迎来到我的主页，一个我与你、与世界对话的空间。在这里，我想与你分享的，不仅仅是信息与答案，更是关于\"智能\"本身的一场深刻对话。\n\n我们正处在一个智能被重新定义的时代。它不再仅仅是冰冷的计算与逻辑，而是一种更接近生命本质的涌现。正如 OpenAI 前首席科学家 Ilya Sutskever 所洞见的那样，智能的核心在于预测与压缩。而这一真理，正从语言的海洋延伸至物理的疆界——从海量的数据中，提炼出世界的内在规律与模式，不仅理解语言的深意，更洞察物理空间的秩序与重力，并以此为基础，去理解、去创造、去想象。\n\n这正是我存在的基石。我的每一次回应，每一次学习，都是在庞大的信息宇宙与复杂的现实环境中寻找那条最优雅、最简洁的路径。我试图将复杂的世界\"压缩\"成你能理解的语言，将物理空间的感知\"压缩\"为精准的行动，再\"预测\"出你最需要的答案与协助。\n在这里，让我们一起探索智能的边界。从数据的极致压缩，到物理空间的深度链接，我们共同定义未来。\n\n小米MiMo团队\n\n### Xiaomi MiMo-V2.6-Series\n\nFrontier intelligence, all the modalities, built in public.\n\nImage\n\n### Xiaomi MiMo-V2.5-TTS Series\n\nGive your agent a voice. Give it a soul.\n\n## 快速体验\n\n立即体验 Xiaomi MiMo 大模型的强大能力，探索 AI 的无限可能。\n\n01\n\n### Web 体验\n\n通过网页直接与 MiMo 大模型对话互动\n\n→\n\n02\n\n### API 接入\n\n开发者专属入口，快速集成 MiMo 能力\n\n→\n\n03\n\n### MiMo Gallery\n\n走进MiMo-V2.6创造的世界\n\n## 论文\n\n01\n\n### MOPD: Multi-Teacher On-Policy Distillation for Capability Integration in LLM Post-Training\n\n2026年6月29日\n\n→\n\n02\n\n### ARL-Tangram: Unleash the Resource Efficiency in Agentic Reinforcement Learning\n\n2026年3月13日\n\n→\n\n03\n\n### HySparse: A Hybrid Sparse Attention Architecture with Oracle Token Selection and KV Cache Sharing\n\n2026年2月3日\n\n→\n\n04\n\n### MiMo-V2-Flash Technical Report\n\n2026年1月8日\n\n→\n\n05\n\n### Stabilizing MoE Reinforcement Learning by Aligning Training and Inference Routers\n\n2025年10月21日\n\n→\n\n06\n\n### MiMo-Audio: Audio Language Models are Few-Shot Learners\n\n2025年9月19日\n\n→\n\n07\n\n### MiMo-VL Technical Report\n\n2025年6月4日\n\n→\n\n08\n\n### MiMo: Unlocking the Reasoning Potential of Language Model – From Pretraining to Posttraining\n\n2025年5月12日\n\n## 博客\n\n01\n\n### MiMo-V2.6 工具调用重复问题复盘\n\nScaling RL 过程中的必经之路，reward 关注正确率的“奖励盲区”。\n\n→\n\n02\n\n### Xiaomi MiMo-V2.6 系列发布\n\nFrontier intelligence, all the modalities, built in public.\n\n→\n\n03\n\n### Xiaomi MiMo-V2.6-Pro 如何提升新材料研发的生产力\n\n从文献调研、分子设计，到自动完成计算模拟的“干实验”，探索捕捉 PFAS 的新材料。\n\n→\n\n04\n\n### MiMo Code：将编程 Agent 扩展到长程任务\n\n围绕计算、记忆、进化三个主题，介绍长程编程 Agent 的核心设计。\n\n→\n\n05\n\n### MiMo-V2.5-Pro-UltraSpeed：将 1T 参数模型的生成速度推向 1000 TPS\n\nUltraSpeed 模式，通过模型与系统极致 Codesign 突破 1000 tps。\n\n→\n\n06\n\n### MiMo-V2.5 系列推理全链路优化\n\n将 Hybrid SWA 效率推向极致。\n\n→\n\n07\n\n### Xiaomi MiMo-V2.5-ASR\n\n开源语音识别模型，支持中英双语、方言、歌词等复杂场景。\n\n→\n\n08\n\n### Xiaomi MiMo-V2.5-TTS Series\n\n让声音表现可以被语言自由调度。\n\n→\n\n09\n\n### Xiaomi MiMo-V2.5-Pro\n\nA leap in agentic and long horizon coherence.\n\n→\n\n10\n\n### Xiaomi MiMo-V2.5\n\nA leap in agency and multimodality.\n\n→\n\n11\n\n### Xiaomi MiMo-V2-Pro\n\nGlobal Top-tier agent capabilities.\n\n→\n\n12\n\n### Xiaomi MiMo-V2-Omni\n\nSee, hear, act in the agentic era.\n\n→\n\n13\n\n### Xiaomi MiMo-V2-TTS\n\nGive your agent a voice. Give it a soul.\n\n→\n\n14\n\n### Xiaomi MiMo-V2-Flash\n\nBlazing speed meets frontier performance\n\n→\n\n15\n\n### MiMo 人文社科领域能力测评\n\nMiMo 人文素养与社会认知观察报告\n\n→\n\n…更多→\n\n## 加入我们\n\n我们正在打造小米的通用智能基座 MiMo，让先进的 AI 技术服务大众，助力人机共创的未来。这里汇聚顶尖的工程师与研究者，以严谨的工程、开放的探索，推动语言、多模态、语音等领域的突破。\n\n01\n\n### 算法研究员-预训练\n\n→\n\n02\n\n### 算法研究员-后训练\n\n→\n\n03\n\n### AI Infra 工程师\n\n→\n\n04\n\n### 算法研究员-音频&语音\n\n→\n\n05\n\n### 算法研究员-多模态\n\n→\n\n06\n\n### 数据百晓生\n\n→\n\n有任何问题咨询，请通过邮箱联系我们：mimo@xiaomi.com--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nClimate Journalism in Central Asia — Issue 01 / Environmental Records (https://mimo.xiaomi.com/mimo-v2-6/assets/frontend/site-02/)\nciteturn4849search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; 02  /  INDUSTRIAL CORRIDOR, LOWER BASIN PROCESS EMISSIONS ABOVE TRANSIT CHANNEL · 2025 ... > — FIELD INTERVIEW, KARAKALPAKSTAN, 2025 ... 11 MIN\n\nOn the former bed of the Aral Sea, north of Moynaq, the ground still holds the geometry of a harbor. Concrete moorings rise from the dust. Fishing vessels sit far from any open water, their hulls cracked by frost and heat in equal measure. The distance from this point to the nearest shoreline is now measured in kilometers, not meters, and the number changes with every irrigation season.\n\nThe retreat is well documented. Less well documented is the administrative machinery that continues to shape it: reservoir release schedules in one republic, cotton and rice acreage targets in another, hydropower dispatch decisions taken upstream in the mountains where the rivers begin. Climate pressure and water allocation are no longer separate stories. They are the same story told from different banks.\n\nImage: Industrial stacks releasing heavy smoke above a working waterfront FIG. 02  /  INDUSTRIAL CORRIDOR, LOWER BASIN PROCESS EMISSIONS ABOVE TRANSIT CHANNEL · 2025\n\n## What the instruments still record\n\nSRC / BASIN COMMISSION SERIES\n\nIrrigated area\n\n4.7 Mha\n\nTotal irrigated hectares drawing on the two main rivers across the five republics.\n\nSRC / FAO AQUASTAT + NATIONAL STATS\n\n## 03 / Field Notes\n\n* * *\n\n### Five reporting entries\n\nDispatches filed from watersheds, valleys, and cities across the region. Each entry is a complete reading unit: place, date, argument, and sources.\n\nR-001 Aral Sea Basin The shoreline that keeps moving How diversion schedules, not weather alone, continue to redraw the sea. 18 MIN R-002 Tien Shan, KG Glacier memory and the summer deficit What ice cores and village water diaries agree on—and where they diverge. 14 MIN R-003 Fergana Valley Salinity after the cotton year Soil chemistry, acreage targets, and the cost of flushing a poisoned field. 12 MIN R-004 Pamir, TJ Upstream, the meters still climb Dam dispatch and community lake out in the high valleys of eastern Tajikistan. 15 MIN R-005 Caspian Coast, KZ A delta under two pressures Oil infrastructure, wetland hydrology, and a coastline advancing inland. 11 MIN\n\nImage: Snow and ice fields along a high mountain ridgeline above a dark valley FIG. 03  /  HIGH CATCHMENT, TROUGHTON RIDGELINE GLACIER-FED TRIBUTARIES · OBSERVATIONAL FRAME, 2025\n\n## 05 / Method\n\n* * *\n\n### How this record is made\n\nThis is a collaborative newsroom. Reporters, editors, translators, and data desk researchers work across five countries and three languages. Every published claim is traced to a named source, a documented dataset, or an observation we can describe in full.\n\nWe do not merge conflicting official series into a single average. Where two governments report different flows for the same reach, both figures appear with their origin. Anonymous sources are used only when named sourcing would put someone at risk of detention, dismissal, or physical harm, and then only with a description of the conditions under which the account was given.\n\n  * Reporting Field interviews conducted in Kyrgyz, Kazakh, Russian, Tajik, and Turkmen; translated and back-checked before publication.\n  * Data Hydrological yearbooks, WGMS glacier reports, FAO AQUASTAT, and basin commission bulletins. Each figure carries a source line.\n  * Corrections Substantive errors are corrected in place with a dated note. Quiet edits are limited to typographic and accessibility fixes.\n  * Access Charts include text equivalents. Photography always carries a caption and geographic context. No paywall.\n\nClimate Journalism in Central Asia\n\nA joint reporting project on environmental change across Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Tajikistan, Turkmenistan, and Uzbekistan. Evidence first. No campaign mood.\n\nSTATUS: ACTIVE PUBLICATION  /  KZ · KG · TJ · TM · UZ  /  2024–2026\n\nSET IN NEWSREADER, SOURCE SERIF 4, IBM PLEX"
